---
layout: article
title: Start with Analytics
description: Track your first website visit with Appwrite Analytics. Create a property, add the Web SDK's tracking helper to your site, and see the visit on the dashboard.
difficulty: beginner
readtime: 5
---

In this quick start you create an analytics property, add tracking to a website with the Appwrite Web SDK, and see your first visit on the dashboard.

# Add your site to the project {% #add-web-app %}

Appwrite accepts events from a browser only when the site's hostname belongs to one of the project's apps. If your site isn't one yet, add it.

1. Sign in to [Appwrite Cloud](https://cloud.appwrite.io) and open a project.
2. Open **Apps** in the sidebar and click **Add app**.
3. Choose **Web**, enter your site's hostname, such as `example.com`, and finish the wizard.

Add `localhost` the same way to track your site while you develop.

# Create a property {% #create-property %}

{% only_dark %}
![Create property page with a name, a domain, and the Web platform selected](/images/docs/analytics/dark/create-property.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Create property page with a name, a domain, and the Web platform selected](/images/docs/analytics/create-property.avif)
{% /only_light %}

A property collects the events of one site or app.

1. Open **Analytics** in the sidebar and click **Create property**.
2. Enter a **Name**, such as `Acme Store`.
3. Enter your site's **Domain**, such as `example.com`.
4. Keep **Web** selected under **Platform**.
5. Click **Create property**.

The Console opens the install screen and waits for your site's first event.

# Add tracking to your site {% #add-tracking %}

Install the Web SDK in your site's project.

```sh
npm install appwrite
```

Add this code so it runs once in the browser when your site loads, for example in the entry file of your app or in a component at its root. The install screen shows the same setup with your endpoint, project ID, and property ID filled in.

```client-web
import { Client, Analytics, Tracking } from 'appwrite';

const client = new Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>');

const tracking = new Tracking(new Analytics(client), '<PROPERTY_ID>');

tracking.start();
```

`start()` records pageviews, outbound link clicks, scroll depth, and engagement time.

# See your first visit {% #first-visit %}

{% only_dark %}
![Install tracking screen confirming that a pageview event was received](/images/docs/analytics/dark/install-tracking.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Install tracking screen confirming that a pageview event was received](/images/docs/analytics/install-tracking.avif)
{% /only_light %}

Open your site in a browser. Within a few seconds, the install screen shows **Event received** with the first `pageview`.

Click **Open dashboard** to see the visit, with its page, source, location, browser, and device.

